            "review_title": "Review at Letimo Bakery&Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Andy van den Dobbelsteen\nDelft, The Netherlands291 contributions\n0\n5-star vegetarian food, in a peaceful oasis\nJul 2016 • Family\nWe had a wonderful breakfast at Letimo restaurant (also called Mây) and came back later in the evening for supper. It is a place of peace and quiet (a Buddhist feel) in a hectic part of Nha Trang, with friendly, relaxed staff. Letimo has a great range of croissants, pain au chocolat, pastry and cakes on display in front of the restaurant (their bakery is superb) but passers-by should really try the menu indoors as well. For breakfast we had yoghurt with muesli and fresh fruit, freshly pressed fruit juice, the best espresso and tea. Their vegetarian menu for lunch and supper is extensive. The tasty dishes we had are just the best around; even carnivores should try the mock meat and fish and realise that vegetarian food can be so good, with no animals hurt. Absolute 5 star quality!\nRead more\nWritten July 29, 2016",
